PRACTICE — lesson 05: from CSV to answers with SQLite
-----------------------------------------------------
/work/orders.csv holds ten orders of a small online shop. The first
line is the header: id,day,city,total. Don't change orders.csv.

1. Create /work/shop.db with a table orders and load all ten orders
   into it. id must be stored as an integer and total as a real
   number (check with typeof), and the header must not become a row.
2. Write /work/top.csv: one line per city with the number of orders
   and the sum of total rounded to 2 decimals, biggest sum first,
   with the header line city,orders,total.

Check: sh /practice/check.sh     Answer: /practice/solution.md
[exit 0]

# check PRZED rozwiązaniem (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  orders.csv is unchanged
FAIL  /work/shop.db does not exist yet
FAIL  /work/top.csv does not exist yet

RESULT: FAIL (2 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ cd /work && sqlite3 shop.db "CREATE TABLE orders(id INTEGER, day TEXT, city TEXT, total REAL)" && sqlite3 shop.db ".import --csv --skip 1 orders.csv orders"

[exit 0]

# check po CZĘŚCI rozwiązania (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  orders.csv is unchanged
PASS  orders has 10 rows, id is integer, total is real, no header row
FAIL  /work/top.csv does not exist yet

RESULT: FAIL (1 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ cd /work && sqlite3 -header -csv shop.db "SELECT city, COUNT(*) AS orders, ROUND(SUM(total), 2) AS total FROM orders GROUP BY city ORDER BY total DESC" > top.csv

[exit 0]

